<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  =========================================================================
  File        : network_security_config.xml   (debug builds only)
  Project     : Smart Solar Microgrid Trading System - SE4040 Assignment 1
  Author      : NIMSARA R V P P (IT 23215306)
  Created     : 2026-09-29
  Description : Lets a debug build talk to the Web API over plain HTTP.

  Why this file is in src/debug
                Android merges resources, and a file here replaces the one
                of the same name in src/main for debug builds only. So the
                release build keeps the strict rule and never sees this.

  Why it is not a list of hosts any more
                It used to name each laptop IP. That meant the address was
                written in two places, here and in the Java, and changing
                only one gave the error:
                    CLEARTEXT communication to ... not permitted

                The address now lives in local.properties alone. This file
                cannot read that, so instead of repeating it, a debug build
                simply allows plain HTTP and the address is checked in one
                place only.

  Is that safe
                A debug build is not something anyone installs from a store.
                It is signed with the debug key, it is not shipped, and it
                already permits the debugger to read everything in the app.
                Allowing plain HTTP in it gives away nothing that was not
                already open.

                The release build is the one that matters, and it now
                refuses plain HTTP altogether. That is stricter than the
                named list it replaced.
  =========================================================================
-->
<network-security-config>

    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />

</network-security-config>
